<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gleb of Ryazan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1178">1178</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Gleb Rostislavich</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gleb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a> (Gleb Rostislavich) was prince of Ryazan from about 1145 to 1177. In the succession struggle for Vladimir after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrei-bogolyubsky">Andrei Bogolyubsky</a>'s murder he backed his brothers-in-law against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vsevolod-the-big-nest">Vsevolod the Big Nest</a>, and his forces burned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> in 1177. That year Vsevolod defeated him on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koloksha">Koloksha</a> River and took him prisoner; he died in captivity in Vladimir in 1178.</p></div>
